    },
    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Organizations contain projects and centralize billing and teams. Projects separate environments, cluster configurations, network settings, and database-user credentials. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/organizations-projects.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a9d4b98afbbd648108ca1413ff392f457886a9a922253b6d30d2cf9e060e8c01",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:805de02535270035a8bac6f2b373a937f540807d27ed6041e3fe8ea203956504"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/user-roles.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Organizations contain projects, and clusters belong to projects. Organization-level billing retains project usage visibility. Separate projects can isolate environments, credentials, and security configurations; this makes the project a meaningful security boundary. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/organizations-projects.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2b53cb305012bca28483b2931e1f20d8741f543612cb87cdc4365f4bca789b73",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:66bb54c30530eaa3f4a89988f3358e68b264d506958b281a1398cb777db24980"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/user-roles.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Organization Owner inherits Project Owner authority across the organization, including database access, even when explicitly assigned a weaker project role. These inherited owners are absent from the project access list. Auditing only that list can therefore miss privileged users. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/user-roles.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:09c83cd8a6a75858635be63d22a48058ed9fa17979c6b1d6c77ee159532bc5d4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:60f757ea3f3a59addade2ec8c9ac4de56e8b2e228e0fdca332d70c55bf28dc65"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Separate identity stores do not prevent management-plane data access: Project Owner includes Data Explorer access, and project data-access roles can authorize database operations through the UI. Review these permissions when separating operators from data readers. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/user-roles.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5143f0ab6a7755147508661999c75bbb87c41dfde05f46211e0ff64b63e67e5c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:696399a8cfafb333e55e33c85dc4e9ae62e917f82f5a8f999f1857ffc1d18e56",
            "ev:7f71adb924401b675c1b4ec1690528a188db0ad1793cf4c62db4fa2d28a8b01b"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/organizations-projects.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Database users belong to a project and, by default, can access its clusters and federated database instances subject to their roles. Restrict Access to Specific Clusters/Federated Database Instances narrows deployment scope; database roles further limit permitted operations and resources. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:85ecd55462f258e2090bd6fed1ef919c41ceb74e9edee46ddede7d035bcd1da8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:893df4b4b9e8c50dcbfa0faf68b575d12af8bc877417bbde30109b44e6e5c7f1",
            "ev:f3b3abc4553364b3a2089184b85e17e6947fd599314954ae41bc886319df8364"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://docs.atlan.com/apps/connectors/database/mongodb/how-tos/set-up-mongodb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Project Database Access Admin can manage database users and custom database roles without directly granting Data Explorer access. This distinguishes credential administration from direct UI data access; it does not prove that credential administrators cannot obtain data access indirectly. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/user-roles.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:35793cfe0fbfab90341419b17927290b7ea78b611b74d5db48b54656d3f18cee",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8bfccff1589419a898585f6ac3be1caeb5901425d8f7935a348ab6d8a2fcd6ca"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Manage Atlas database users through supported Atlas interfaces. MongoDB documents Atlas CLI support, including atlas dbusers list. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md",
          "note": null,
